{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":850758,"duration_api_ms":903689,"num_turns":99,"result":"Now let me produce the JSON response. Let me summarize all the changes:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Introduced chloride-aware nitrite hazard modifier using the formula: effective_hazard = [NO2] / (1 + chloride_protection_factor × [Cl] / [NO2]). The chloride_protection_factor is a named species parameter (default 0.5 for Neocaridina davidi), calibrated so Cl:NO2 > 10:1 yields < 20% of unprotected hazard. The effective hazard replaces raw nitrite concentration in both the hourly nitrite stress accumulation path and the daily condition update nitrite_factor, integrating directly into the existing stress/mortality accounting rather than creating a parallel toxicology system. Nitrite warning events now expose NO2, Cl, Cl:NO2 ratio, and effective hazard for diagnosability. Seven unit tests verify monotonic hazard reduction, zero-nitrite safety, protection ratio thresholds, species parameter configurability, and integration with the existing hourly_nitrite_stress_accum pathway. One integration test models a salt-treatment emergency scenario confirming reduced mortality when chloride is raised despite persistent elevated nitrite.\",\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    \"chloride_protection_factor scalar (0.5) is calibrated to directional literature support and the Cl:NO2 > 10:1 < 20% criterion, not to species-specific LC50 data; confidence is medium\",\n    \"The formula treats chloride protection as instantaneous; real gill uptake competition has kinetic lag that is not modeled\",\n    \"Pre-existing saves without chloride_protection_factor will deserialize with the serde default (0.5), which changes nitrite stress behavior for tanks that already had chloride present — this is the intended behavior but could surprise users comparing old vs new runs\"\n  ],\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added chloride_mg_per_l() accessor methods to WaterState and ConcentrationView in water.rs\",\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added chloride_protection_factor field to ShrimpRuntimeParams in biology.rs with serde default (0.5), doc comment explaining formula and confidence level, and updated Default impl\",\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added chloride_protection_factor to ShrimpPreset in presets.rs including validation, lookup_param_value, has_param_named, and shrimp_runtime_default_param_value\",\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Wired chloride_protection_factor through shrimp_preset_to_params in tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs\",\n      \"order\": 4,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added chloride_protection_factor = 0.5 to neocaridina_davidi.toml species data with updated provenance notes\",\n      \"order\": 5,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added pub fn compute_effective_nitrite_hazard() in shrimp.rs implementing the Cl-aware hazard formula with documented properties and confidence level\",\n      \"order\": 6,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Modified step_hourly_shrimp_stress() to use effective nitrite hazard (with chloride protection) instead of raw nitrite for the hourly_nitrite_stress_accum pathway\",\n      \"order\": 7,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Modified update_condition() to use effective nitrite hazard for the nitrite_factor in daily condition calculation\",\n      \"order\": 8,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Updated nitrite warning event in events.rs to expose NO2, Cl, Cl:NO2 ratio, and effective hazard in the summary string for diagnosability\",\n      \"order\": 9,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added 6 unit tests: test_chloride_reduces_nitrite_hazard (monotonic decrease), test_chloride_protection_ratio (Cl:NO2 > 10:1 < 20%), test_zero_nitrite_zero_hazard, test_protection_factor_is_species_parameter, test_stress_accounting_integrates_with_existing, test_high_nitrite_low_chloride_vs_high_chloride\",\n      \"order\": 10,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added integration test test_salt_treatment_emergency_scenario: cycling crash with high NO2, verifies mortality is high before salt treatment and measurably lower after raising chloride while NO2 remains elevated\",\n      \"order\": 11,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Verified all tests pass (cargo test), no clippy warnings (cargo clippy), and code is formatted (cargo fmt --check)\",\n      \"order\": 12,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validation_evidence\": [\n    \"cargo test: all 84 unit tests + 159 integration/e2e tests pass (0 failures)\",\n    \"cargo clippy: no warnings on changed code\",\n    \"cargo fmt --check: all changed files formatted correctly\",\n    \"test_chloride_reduces_nitrite_hazard: confirms monotonic hazard decrease from 1.0 (no Cl) through [5, 10, 20, 30, 50, 100] mg/L Cl\",\n    \"test_chloride_protection_ratio: at Cl:NO2=10:1 with cpf=0.5, effective hazard = 0.167 which is < 20% of unprotected (1.0)\",\n    \"test_zero_nitrite_zero_hazard: zero nitrite returns zero hazard regardless of chloride (0, 50, 200 mg/L)\",\n    \"test_protection_factor_is_species_parameter: different cpf values (0.2 vs 0.8) produce different hazards; parameter exists as named field in ShrimpRuntimeParams\",\n    \"test_stress_accounting_integrates_with_existing: chloride modification feeds into hourly_nitrite_stress_accum (same accumulator), not a parallel system\",\n    \"test_high_nitrite_low_chloride_vs_high_chloride: 5 mg/L NO2 with 0 Cl produces >3x more nitrite stress than same NO2 with 100 mg/L Cl over 24h\",\n    \"test_salt_treatment_emergency_scenario: 7-day run with 20 shrimp at 4 mg/L NO2 — no-salt scenario has more deaths than salt-treated (100 mg/L Cl) scenario, and nitrite remains elevated >0.5 mg/L in both\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ca1f392f-4a14-4513-80a1-141b648a9aca","total_cost_usd":7.036491300000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":886,"cache_creation_input_tokens":150872,"cache_read_input_tokens":9821168,"output_tokens":31111,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":150872,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":167,"outputTokens":18250,"cacheReadInputTokens":1246953,"cacheCreationInputTokens":147712,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.40075230000000006,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":886,"outputTokens":31111,"cacheReadInputTokens":9821168,"cacheCreationInputTokens":150872,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":6.635739000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f8a7292a-d040-41bf-8099-f16415369875"}
